(commit fef96fad0c54547637dd2bbdc326450027a906e7)

Codex Dev changed the following when building inspector.js and inspector.css:

  - Renamed the custom elements, identifiers and file names to Codex Dev names.
  - Restyled the toolbar: horizontal, docked at the bottom of the window,
    Codex Dev colors and spacing, Tabler line icons (MIT) instead of the
    original icon set.
  - Tooltips show text only; the tutorial animations are not included.
  - Empty color pickers use the toolbar icon color.
  - Toolbar buttons only respond to clicks; the grip is the only drag
    handle, and dragged panels stop following the cursor once the mouse
    button is released.
  - Closing the toolbar runs every cleanup step even if one fails, and
    removes any overlays and selection marks left on the page.
  - The Text, Background and Border colour swatches have keyboard shortcuts
    (T, B, R to switch, C to cycle, press the active key again to open the
    picker), shown in their hover cards.
  - Built from the toolbar component instead of the demo site entry file,
    as a classic script that defines its elements only once per page.
  - The AI button group is hidden when the page sets window.__codexAiOff
    (set by the extension from ai/feature-flags.js).
